+ΔW = 2(√γ_A − √γ_S)² ≥ 0
+; the small SE phase keeps like–like contacts best, so uncoated beds can retain SE–SE clusters.
+Uniformly cohesive runs keep most SE in SE–SE clusters after two revolutions, unlike the run without NCM–NCM cohesion; the 
+confirmatory 18-run block stays on hold
