+This work — exploratory runs (left) · ratified thesis argument (right)
+Left: one seed, averaged over the second revolution; whiskers = dump-resolution range. Right: work-of-adhesion argument (γ = surface energy,
+W = work of adhesion, R* = reduced radius, ρ = density of the smaller particle); the uncoated NCM / SE surface-energy ratio is not known.
+Sources: docs/hetero_thesis.md (ratified 2026-10-05) §2-1 · §2-2 · §2-8: W_ij ≈ 2√(γ_i γ_j); ΔW = W_AA + W_SS − 2 W_AS = 2(√γ_A − √γ_S)² ≥ 0; pair Bond number ∝ W·R*/(ρ g R³) of the smaller particle — at equal surface energy the SE–SE pair Bond number is about 194× that of the large-NCM pair and SE→NCM adhesion is 1.8× SE–SE (arithmetic estimates); for SE–SE clusters to survive in an uncoated bed the ratio γ_NCM/γ_SE would have to be below about 0.31 — that ratio is not known (open decision). Predictions P1–P3 of the thesis: uncoated beds keep SE–SE clustering above random; coating removes it; the mixing difference carries into the compacted SE pathway. The present cohesion model does not yet contain that mechanism (NCM–NCM cohesion was varied, not SE–SE). Left figure: docs/data/mixer_highbo_devu_prelim_20261006/README.md §3 — fraction of SE in SE–SE clusters (bin 1, after two revolutions): 0.401 [0.143, 0.542] without NCM–NCM cohesion; 0.954 [0.875, 0.957] all pairs ×10; 0.988 [0.981, 0.988] all pairs ×14 (ranges = dump-resolution [certain, possible]; difference only where ranges do not overlap; one seed; development data). Confirmatory 18-run block: registered, on hold after the Codex rounds (docs/reviews/mixer_highbo_prereg_20260927.md); no "real coating effect" sentence.--- v2/[17]
